{
  "note": [
    "The site dressing kit (P02f): one trim sheet that every small prop of the kit shares (sacks, pallets, drums, chairs, hoses, pipe, umbrella, hard hat, desk things), one cut-out sheet for the fence, and one sheet of decals (ground storytelling and weathering). Read by scripts/twin/build-atlases.mjs, which paints them, and by scripts/blender/twin/model_kit.py and build_gate_dressing.py, which map faces onto them.",
    "Trim bands as in gate.json. `prints` are rectangles [x, y, w, h] in pixels from the top-left of the sheet, drawn over the band named `print` (labels, a calendar, an open logbook).",
    "A decal sheet has an alpha channel and is drawn blended over what is under it (materials named DECAL_..., engine/assets.ts). Its bands tile along U like a trim sheet's; its `rects` are single stamps."
  ],
